The widget now shows more of your clocks before it starts hiding any: it drops to compact rows first, and only then sets aside a zone whose time is already on screen. Whenever something is hidden it says so, so you can tell you are looking at part of the list.

When two of your places keep the same time, the one you named — Mississauga rather than a bare zone — is the one that stays.

Renaming a place that shares a zone with one you already saved now sticks.
